\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Eternal Light eternal Light!
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj How pure the soul must be,
\par When, placed within Thy searching sight,
\par It shrinks not, but, with calm delight,
\par can live , and look on Thee!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  The spirit that surround Thy throne
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj May bear the burning bliss;
\par But that is surely theirs alone,
\par    Since they have never, never known
\par   A fallen world like this.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  O how shall I, whose native sphere
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0 Is dark, whose mind is dim,
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0  Before the Ineffable appear,
\par  And on my naked spirit bear
\par   The uncreated beam?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   There is a way for man to rise
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  To that sublime abode:
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   An offering and a sacrifice\tab\tab 
\par  A holy spirit's  energies,
\par  An Advocate with God.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. These, these prepare us for the sight
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0  Of holiness above:
\par  The sons of ignorance and night
\par  May dwell in the eternal Light,
\par  Through the eternal Love!
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

